s of Oct 12, the record for Tensas Parish runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years, more than any other pair, and it is also the driest pair at 6.83 inches. In 2025, November to December finished at 37% of normal on the middle of the grids. For 2026 so far, January to February sat at 48% and May to June at 173% on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
